msgid "``em.host`` — the hosts (EMStudio, EM Tools, a script)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generated for em API |api| from the docstrings of :mod:`s3dgraphy.em.host`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The host — what EMStudio and Blender implement, and the one with no application."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em`` imports neither ``bpy`` nor anything of EMStudio: the host REGISTERS (:func:`install`). It gives the common half what only an application knows — which graph is open, who is working, which caller is writing, how a delta becomes a step — and the application half, ``em.app`` (SPEC-plugin §2.4)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Without a host (``python -c …``, a script, a test) the current host is a :class:`ScriptHost`: the «no application» host of the command line. Its graph is the one a script opened (``em.open(path)``) or handed over (``em.use(g)``); it applies a delta with :func:`s3dgraphy.contract.apply_delta_to_graph`, the same seam as everywhere; its ``app`` answers every call with :class:`~s3dgraphy.em.errors.NotAvailable` («no application»)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Who writes is the host's to say, never the script's**: :meth:`Host.author` is the identity of the session (``editorHand()`` in EMStudio, EM Tools' in Blender; for the command line the ``author=`` the session was opened with, or ``S3DGRAPHY_AUTHOR``); :meth:`Host.caller` is the descriptor of whoever is calling (the console, a plugin's command). ``em.write`` takes neither."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bases: :py:class:`~typing.Protocol`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The application half (``em.app``). A host that lacks an idea raises :class:`NotAvailable` for it — the same shape where the idea exists in both applications, absent where it does not (SPEC §2.4)."
msgstr ""

